    not_duplicate_of: []  # e42e
    pr_ref:  # e42e
    description: "Discovered while comparing deep-20260407-030917 (pre-fix) vs deep-20260407-050552 (post-fix WI-tutob/WI-supih/WI-puvab). The compare output shows:\\n\\nSession A: deep-20260407-030917 (hash: 89c27393bdec)\\nSession B: deep-20260407-050552 (hash: a285771e7012)\\nCode: different\\n\\nRepo                      Verdict          orphan  avg_slice cross_fileR centrality    LLM\\nalertmanager              GOOD               0.0       0.0       0.0       0.0 +  3.0\\nkserve                    GOOD               0.0       0.0       0.0       0.0 +  1.3\\nprometheus                WARN->GOOD         0.0       0.0       0.0       0.0 +  1.7\\n\\nAggregate deltas (B - A, mean):\\n  orphan_rate: 0.00\\n  avg_slice_nodes: 0.00\\n  cross_file_ratio: 0.00\\n  centrality_gini: 0.00\\n  LLM overall: +2.00\\n\\nThe metric deltas are ALL zero, even though prometheus genuinely had structural slice changes (the verdict change WARN→GOOD on LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO required slice_access_mode_coverage to flip from <50% to ≥50%). The LLM delta is captured (+2.00 mean), so the reflect-comparison path works. Only the metric-comparison path is broken.\\n\\nLikely root cause: field name mismatch (the compare script reads metrics from one path/key in state.json or report.yaml that doesn't match where the metrics actually live), or a no-op aggregation that always produces 0. Investigate scripts/bakeoff-deep compare implementation around the metric-loading and delta-computation logic.\\n\\nReproduce: `./scripts/bakeoff-deep compare deep-20260407-030917 deep-20260407-050552`. The metric values themselves are present and correct in each session's diag/cohort-001/iter-001/report.yaml — the bug is purely in how compare reads them."  # e42e
    fields: {}  # e42e
- op: discuss  # 9818
  at: '2026-04-07T10:48:29Z'  # 9818
  by: agent  # 9818
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9818
  clock: 2  # 9818
  nonce: '9818'  # 9818
  message: "CORRECTION on initial analysis. The compare script is NOT broken — verified by directly loading both report.yaml files:\n\ndeep-20260407-030917 alertmanager: orphan=18.80, slice=88.7, cross=50.72, gini=0.602\ndeep-20260407-050552 alertmanager: orphan=18.80, slice=88.7, cross=50.72, gini=0.602\n[same for kserve and prometheus]\n\nThe metric values are LITERALLY IDENTICAL between sessions. The 0.0 deltas are correct.\n\nBut here's the more interesting finding: prometheus VERDICT changed WARN → GOOD even though all four displayed metrics are identical. The verdict change is real but invisible from the compare output. Why? Because the WI-tutob fix added a NEW threshold-suppression metric (slice_access_mode_coverage) that the compare script doesn't display. When slice_access_mode_coverage ≥ 50%, the LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO WARN is suppressed even when the underlying ratio is unchanged.\n\nSo the actual issue is the compare script's KEY_METRICS list is too narrow — it shows orphan_rate / avg_slice_nodes / cross_file_ratio / centrality_gini but not slice_access_mode_coverage / dataflow_slice_ratio / slice_coverage_pct / tier1_pct / etc. This makes verdict-change explanations opaque.\n\nREVISED TITLE: 'bakeoff-deep compare: KEY_METRICS list missing newer fields, hides verdict-change explanations'\n\nREVISED FIX: extend key_metrics in cmd_compare (scripts/bakeoff-deep:3042) to include the metrics that drive verdict changes — slice_access_mode_coverage, dataflow_slice_ratio, slice_coverage_pct, tier1_pct, io_tag_rate. Or even simpler: derive key_metrics dynamically from the union of metric keys present in the two sessions, ranked by absolute delta.\n\nDemoting from defect to enhancement. Still useful but not actually a bug — the compare faithfully reports zero deltas on the metrics it knows about."  # 9818
